# Saved-run storage contract v1

This document records the storage contract introduced for v0.6 PR 1. The CLI
now creates records through opt-in `--orchestrate --save-run` and inspects them
through `--list-runs` / `--show-run <run-id>`. `--resume <run-id>` continues
eligible clean stops after a fresh review and preflight.
Saved records are never executable instructions or approved candidates.

## Files and bounds

The default store is outside the repository:

- Windows: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\dev-orchestrator\\saved-runs`, falling back to
  `%USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\\dev-orchestrator\\saved-runs`.
- macOS: `~/Library/Application Support/dev-orchestrator/saved-runs`.
- Other Unix systems: `$XDG_STATE_HOME/dev-orchestrator/saved-runs`, falling
  back to `~/.local/state/dev-orchestrator/saved-runs`.

The store contains `runs/<uuid>/checkpoint.json`,
`runs/<uuid>/events.jsonl`, a clean-stop `runs/<uuid>/repository.json` sidecar,
and ownership files under `locks/`. It is rejected
when located inside the selected worker-writable repository. Run IDs are
version-4 UUIDs; callers cannot choose a path through an ID.

Inspection does not create a missing store, change permissions, write traces,
acquire locks, or remove ownership files. It verifies checkpoint/ledger integrity
before displaying saved data. A present update lock prevents a stable read;
concurrent writes can also produce an integrity error, which is reported
without repair. Run and worktree locks are reported conservatively, since a PID
cannot prove whether ownership is stale. Inspection does not require the
repository to exist or resolve provider credentials.

Listing scans at most 128 store entries and displays at most 20 records, placing
unreadable records first and sorting valid records by update time. Unknown
entry names are counted without displaying them. A store with more than 128
entries refuses listing; `--show-run` still reads a known ID directly. Detail
shows up to 12 recent events. Unreadable records display only the validated ID
and an allowlisted error classification; unverified checkpoint text is never
used as fallback. Listing or showing never grants continuation permission.

| Record | Limit |
| --- | ---: |
| Checkpoint | 1 MiB |
| Event record | 4 KiB |
| Events per run | 128 |
| Runs per store | 128 |
| Orchestration iteration ceiling | 8 |
| Calls per worker | 2 |
| Content snapshot record | 512 KiB |
| Compared paths / bytes per file / total bytes | 512 / 1 MiB / 32 MiB |
| Git file metadata | 32 KiB, using the fixed two-second Git diagnostic deadline |

The v1 checkpoint has exactly these top-level fields: `schemaVersion`,
`runId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `sequence`, `ledgerHead`, `status`,
`iterationLimit`, `repository`, `configuration`, `state`, and `checksum`.
The repository identity contains the canonical worktree root, Git common
directory, full HEAD object ID, and a worktree fingerprint. Configuration
freezes mock/live mode, provider and model identifiers, worker selection, and
Codex network permission. Cloudflare records also contain a SHA-256 fingerprint
of the account ID; the account ID itself is not stored.

`state` is a bounded, validated `AgentState`. Known current environment
credentials are redacted from persisted text. Provider keys, Cloudflare account
IDs, raw environment values, transport objects, abort signals, raw provider
responses, and executable candidates are excluded. Task text and bounded
repository excerpts can still contain sensitive information; the local store
is not encrypted, and pattern-based redaction cannot identify every secret.

No automatic retention or deletion is provided. For manual housekeeping, stop
the CLI and confirm that no process owns the affected run or worktree before
moving/removing an inactive `runs/<uuid>` directory. Preserve both checkpoint
and ledger when retaining a record. Never edit counters, reconstruct a partial
record, or remove an ownership file based only on its PID to force execution.

## Event ledger and ordering

Events use schema version 1 and are stored as one JSON object per newline. Each
event contains a sequence number, timestamp, previous-event hash, immutable run
identity hash, resulting state hash, event data, and SHA-256 event hash. The
checkpoint stores the current sequence and ledger head. Reads reject duplicate
JSON keys, unknown versions, malformed or oversized records, sequence gaps,
hash mismatches, identity changes, and checkpoint/ledger disagreement. No
migration or trace import is defined; unknown versions are inspection failures
and must never be resumed.

The event vocabulary records run creation and continuation, iteration
reservations, completed/failed evaluations, explicit action approvals,
execution reservations and outcomes, clarifications, clean stops, completion,
iteration exhaustion, and blocked states. Validation enforces increasing
iterations, the original ceiling, worker-call limits, exact call-counter
agreement, approval before dispatch, matching execution outcomes, and current
independent validation plus a fresh `FINISH` approval before a finished status.
Stops and continuations discard any outstanding action approval. An unresolved
execution prevents a resumable stop. These checks validate stored history; they
do not replace the orchestration policy or independently establish that task
acceptance criteria were met.

Coding-worker `execution_outcome` events may include a reporting-only `usage`
object: numeric `input`, `output`, and `total`, with optional `cachedInput` and
`cacheWriteInput`. Counts must be nonnegative safe integers no greater than
one trillion, `total` must equal input plus output, and cache components cannot
exceed input. Unknown fields are rejected. The outcome must match a coding
worker reservation. No raw worker event, cost, credential, or model metadata
is saved here, and usage never enters `AgentState` or approved candidates.

History and the CLI's saved-task totals sum this usage once per reserved
worker attempt across all process segments. Missing outcomes or older events
without usage count as unavailable, rather than zero. The optional field does
not alter schema version 1, attempt ordering, budgets, or continuation checks;
older development readers that reject this field require the newer CLI.

New clean-stop events include `repositorySnapshotHash`, the SHA-256 of a
version-1 `repository.json` manifest. The manifest contains bounded relative
paths and content hashes (or null for missing tracked/root context files),
never file contents. It includes tracked and untracked files, even Git-ignored
source. Generated directories `node_modules`, `dist`, `traces`, `.entire`,
`.cache`, `.next`, `.turbo`, `coverage`, and `.venv` are excluded. Secret paths
such as `.env*`, `.npmrc`, `.netrc`, `.ssh`, `.aws`, credential/secret files,
private-key names, and key/certificate extensions are excluded without reading
their contents. Root instruction files and `package.json` are checked even
when absent or ignored. Links, unsafe names, oversize inputs, or concurrent
changes during collection reject the snapshot.

The manifest is flushed and atomically replaced before its stop event and
checkpoint commit. A mismatch, missing sidecar, partial write, or stale sidecar
prevents continuation. Older development records without this optional event
field remain readable but are inspection only. There is no migration or
automatic fingerprint reconstruction. Required final trace writes complete
before a terminal saved transition, so a trace failure cannot manufacture a
clean continuation point.

## Durability and ownership

On POSIX, the store and run directories use mode `0700`, and record and lock
files use `0600`. Writes use a private temporary file, file flush, atomic rename,
and directory flush where supported. Event appends flush the file and parent
directory. A failure between the ledger append and checkpoint replacement can
leave a mismatch; the store rejects that record instead of guessing which
state is current. The store rejects symbolic links and hard-linked record
files. It does not clean up stale locks automatically; an existing owner file
blocks another owner because a PID is not proof that a lock is safe to remove.

On Windows, the implementation requests restrictive creation modes, but
effective access control is inherited from the parent directory and is not
verified or rewritten as an ACL. Directory flushing is skipped because Node's
portable filesystem API does not provide the same supported operation there.
The Windows-specific filesystem and terminal matrix remains part of the later
v0.6 verification milestone; this PR's automated storage tests ran on POSIX.

Exclusive lock files coordinate processes using this store. A run lock keys one
run; a worktree lock keys its canonical root. Lock files are created with
exclusive-create semantics and removed only by their recorded token owner.
External editors and older CLI versions do not participate in these locks.

SHA-256 checks detect corruption and checkpoint-only edits or rollback when
compared with the event ledger. They do not authenticate the operator, protect
against a compromised local account, or detect a coordinated rewrite or
rollback of the entire store. The saved directory must therefore remain under
the operator's control and outside worker-writable repositories.

## Credential continuity decision

Resume freezes the provider and model identifier and reloads the selected
credential from the operator's current environment. It will never save a
credential value or compare a hash of one. Cloudflare's non-secret account ID
can be compared using its stored fingerprint. The other configured providers
expose no non-secret account identity in this client, so continuity for those
credentials cannot be verified. Its review states that limitation and
requires an explicit operator continuation decision;
reloading a credential does not prove that it belongs to the same account.

Provider aliases such as `jev-latest` also do not pin the model implementation
served later. The current schema binds the selected identifier, not a remote
provider deployment or model revision.
import { realpath, stat } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { validationChecks, hasOmittedValidationRequirements } from '../repo/validation.js';
import { SavedRunStore, SavedRunStoreError, type SavedRunStoreErrorCode } from './store.js';
import type { SavedRunCheckpointV1, SavedRunEvent } from './types.js';
import { addWorkerUsage, emptyWorkerUsage, type WorkerUsageSummary } from '../agents/usage.js';

export const SAVED_RUN_LIST_LIMIT = 20;
export const SAVED_RUN_TIMELINE_LIMIT = 12;

type SavedRecord = Awaited<ReturnType<SavedRunStore['readForInspection']>>;

/** Ledger-derived reporting only; absent and unresolved usage stays unavailable. */
export function savedWorkerUsage(events: SavedRunEvent[]): WorkerUsageSummary {
  const summary = emptyWorkerUsage();
  for (const attempt of events) {
    if (attempt.type !== 'execution_reserved' || (attempt.action !== 'CALL_CODEX' && attempt.action !== 'CALL_CLAUDE')) continue;
    const outcome = events.find((event) => event.type === 'execution_outcome' && event.attemptId === attempt.attemptId);
    addWorkerUsage(summary, attempt.action === 'CALL_CODEX' ? 'codex' : 'claude', outcome?.type === 'execution_outcome' ? outcome.usage : undefined);
  }
  return summary;
}

/** Reporting data only; continuation must perform its own preflight and approvals. */
export type SavedRunDetail = {
  kind: 'valid';
  checkpoint: SavedRunCheckpointV1;
  iterationsUsed: number;
  iterationsRemaining: number;
  checks: ReturnType<typeof validationChecks>;
  repositoryAvailable: boolean;
  blockers: string[];
  recoveryRequired: boolean;
  lastFailure?: string;
  lastStop?: string;
  events: SavedRunEvent[];
};

export type SavedRunInspectionError = {
  kind: 'unavailable';
  runId: string;
  code: SavedRunStoreErrorCode;
};

export type SavedRunInspection = SavedRunDetail | SavedRunInspectionError;

export function inspectionErrorText(code: SavedRunStoreErrorCode): string {
  switch (code) {
    case 'not_found': return 'No saved record exists for this ID.';
    case 'invalid_input': return 'The run ID or saved input is invalid.';
    case 'unsupported_version': return 'The saved schema version is unsupported; no migration is available.';
    case 'invalid_record': return 'The saved checkpoint or event history is malformed or incomplete.';
    case 'integrity_failure': return 'The checkpoint and event ledger failed integrity checks; saved state is untrusted.';
    case 'limit_reached': return 'Saved storage exceeds its size/count limits or regular-file constraints (including linked or replaced files).';
    case 'busy': return 'An update lock is present; a write may be active or its ownership unresolved. Retry after owner cleanup.';
    case 'storage_failure': return 'Saved storage is unreadable or contains an unsafe path.';
  }
}

async function repositoryAvailable(checkpoint: SavedRunCheckpointV1): Promise<boolean> {
  try {
    for (const directory of [checkpoint.repository.root, checkpoint.repository.gitCommonDirectory]) {
      if (await realpath(directory) !== directory || !(await stat(directory)).isDirectory()) return false;
    }
    return true;
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
}

const BLOCK_REASONS = {
  checkpoint_invalid: 'The checkpoint was recorded as invalid.',
  repository_changed: 'Repository identity or contents changed at the recorded check.',
  configuration_changed: 'The recorded configuration comparison failed.',
  attempt_unresolved: 'An execution attempt has no trustworthy final outcome.',
  lock_stale: 'An ownership lock was recorded as unresolved.',
  storage_failure: 'A required saved-state write failed.',
} as const;

function summarizeRecord(record: SavedRecord, available: boolean): SavedRunDetail {
  const { checkpoint, events, ownership } = record;
  const newestFirst = [...events].reverse();
  const iterationsUsed = events.filter((event) => event.type === 'iteration_reserved').length;
  const iterationsRemaining = checkpoint.iterationLimit - iterationsUsed;
  const blockers: string[] = [];
  const stop = newestFirst.find((event) => event.type === 'run_stopped');
  const lastEvent = events.at(-1);
  const completed = new Set(events.filter((event) => event.type === 'execution_outcome').map((event) => event.attemptId));
  const unresolved = events.filter((event) => event.type === 'execution_reserved' && !completed.has(event.attemptId));
  const uncertain = events.filter((event) => event.type === 'execution_outcome' && event.outcome === 'uncertain');
  if (checkpoint.status === 'finished') blockers.push('Task completion was approved; this run is inspection only.');
  if (checkpoint.status === 'iteration_limit' || iterationsRemaining === 0) {
    blockers.push('The original iteration budget is exhausted; continuation cannot extend it.');
  }
  if (checkpoint.status === 'active' || checkpoint.status === 'evaluation_failed') {
    blockers.push('No durable clean stop is recorded; active or abruptly exited runs cannot continue.');
  }
  if (lastEvent?.type === 'run_blocked') blockers.push(BLOCK_REASONS[lastEvent.reason]);
  if (stop?.type === 'run_stopped' && !stop.resumable && checkpoint.status === 'blocked') {
    blockers.push(`The recorded ${stop.reason} stop was not marked resumable.`);
  }
  if (checkpoint.status === 'stopped' && stop?.type === 'run_stopped' && !stop.repositorySnapshotHash) {
    blockers.push('This stop predates content fingerprints and remains inspection only; start a new saved run.');
  }
  if (unresolved.length > 0) {
    blockers.push(`${unresolved.length} reserved execution attempt(s) have no outcome; their allowances stay charged.`);
  }
  if (uncertain.length > 0) blockers.push('An execution outcome is uncertain; do not replay the reserved action.');
  if (ownership.run) blockers.push('A run ownership lock is present; the owner may be active or unresolved.');
  if (ownership.worktree) blockers.push('A worktree ownership lock is present; the owner may be active or unresolved.');
  if (!available) blockers.push('The saved repository or Git directory is unavailable at its canonical path.');
  const evaluationFailure = newestFirst.find((event) => event.type === 'evaluation_failed');
  const recoveryRequired = evaluationFailure !== undefined &&
    !events.some((event) => event.type === 'evaluation_completed' && event.sequence > evaluationFailure.sequence);
  const failedEvent = newestFirst.find((event) => event.type === 'evaluation_failed' ||
    (event.type === 'execution_outcome' && event.outcome !== 'succeeded') || event.type === 'run_blocked');
  let lastFailure: string | undefined;
  if (failedEvent?.type === 'evaluation_failed') {
    lastFailure = `Iteration ${failedEvent.iteration}: ${failedEvent.code} at ${failedEvent.stage}/${failedEvent.category}.`;
  } else if (failedEvent?.type === 'execution_outcome') {
    const attempt = events.find((event) => event.type === 'execution_reserved' && event.attemptId === failedEvent.attemptId);
    const failure = checkpoint.state.evidence?.failures.slice().reverse().find((item) =>
      attempt?.type === 'execution_reserved' && item.iteration === attempt.iteration && item.action === attempt.action);
    lastFailure = `${attempt?.type === 'execution_reserved' ? `Iteration ${attempt.iteration}: ${attempt.action}` : 'Execution'} ${failedEvent.outcome}.${failure ? ` ${failure.summary}` : ''}`;
  } else if (failedEvent?.type === 'run_blocked') {
    lastFailure = BLOCK_REASONS[failedEvent.reason];
  }
  if (checkpoint.state.evidence?.repoRefreshRequired) {
    blockers.push('The saved state requires repository refresh before validation can confirm completion.');
  }
  if (hasOmittedValidationRequirements(checkpoint.state)) {
    blockers.push('Validation requirements were omitted; completion remains blocked.');
  }
  return {
    kind: 'valid', checkpoint, iterationsUsed, iterationsRemaining,
    checks: validationChecks(checkpoint.state), repositoryAvailable: available,
    blockers, recoveryRequired,
    ...(lastFailure === undefined ? {} : { lastFailure }),
    ...(stop?.type === 'run_stopped' ? { lastStop: `${stop.reason}; ${stop.resumable ? 'clean continuation point recorded' : 'not resumable'}` } : {}),
    events,
  };
}

export async function inspectSavedRun(store: SavedRunStore | undefined, runId: string): Promise<SavedRunInspection> {
  if (!store) return { kind: 'unavailable', runId, code: 'not_found' };
  try {
    const record = await store.readForInspection(runId);
    const detail = summarizeRecord(record, await repositoryAvailable(record.checkpoint));
    const stop = record.events.at(-1);
    if (stop?.type === 'run_stopped' && stop.repositorySnapshotHash) {
      try { await store.readRepositorySnapshot(runId, stop.repositorySnapshotHash); } catch (error) {
        detail.blockers.push(`Repository comparison evidence is unavailable: ${inspectionErrorText(error instanceof SavedRunStoreError ? error.code : 'storage_failure')}`);
      }
    }
    return detail;
  } catch (error) {
    return { kind: 'unavailable', runId, code: error instanceof SavedRunStoreError ? error.code : 'storage_failure' };
  }
}

export type SavedRunListing = {
  runs: SavedRunInspection[];
  total: number;
  ignoredEntries: number;
  hiddenRuns: number;
};

export async function listSavedRuns(store: SavedRunStore | undefined): Promise<SavedRunListing> {
  if (!store) return { runs: [], total: 0, ignoredEntries: 0, hiddenRuns: 0 };
  const { runIds, ignoredEntries } = await store.listIdsForInspection();
  const runs: SavedRunInspection[] = [];
  // Each record is bounded by the store's byte/event limits. Read sequentially
  // so listing cannot allocate the entire store's raw data at once.
  for (const runId of runIds) runs.push(await inspectSavedRun(store, runId));
  runs.sort((left, right) => {
    // Unreadable records are always visible before recent valid records. Do not
    // trust a malformed checkpoint's timestamp to rank or hide its warning.
    if (left.kind !== right.kind) return left.kind === 'unavailable' ? -1 : 1;
    if (left.kind === 'valid' && right.kind === 'valid') {
      return right.checkpoint.updatedAt.localeCompare(left.checkpoint.updatedAt) ||
        left.checkpoint.runId.localeCompare(right.checkpoint.runId);
    }
    return left.kind === 'unavailable' && right.kind === 'unavailable' ? left.runId.localeCompare(right.runId) : 0;
  });
  return {
    runs: runs.slice(0, SAVED_RUN_LIST_LIMIT), total: runs.length, ignoredEntries,
    hiddenRuns: Math.max(0, runs.length - SAVED_RUN_LIST_LIMIT),
  };
}

export function describeSavedEvent(event: SavedRunEvent): string {
  switch (event.type) {
    case 'iteration_reserved': return `iteration_reserved ${event.iteration}`;
    case 'evaluation_completed': return `evaluation_completed ${event.iteration}`;
    case 'evaluation_failed': return `evaluation_failed ${event.iteration}: ${event.code} at ${event.stage}/${event.category}`;
    case 'action_approved': return `action_approved ${event.iteration}: ${event.action} (${event.decision})`;
    case 'execution_reserved': return `execution_reserved ${event.iteration}: ${event.action}`;
    case 'execution_outcome': return `execution_outcome: ${event.outcome}`;
    case 'clarification_recorded': return `clarification_recorded ${event.iteration}`;
    case 'run_stopped': return `run_stopped: ${event.reason}; resumable=${event.resumable}`;
    case 'run_blocked': return `run_blocked: ${event.reason}`;
    case 'run_resumed': return `run_resumed: segment ${event.segment}`;
    default: return event.type;
  }
}

import {
  describeSavedEvent, inspectionErrorText, SAVED_RUN_TIMELINE_LIMIT, savedWorkerUsage,
  type SavedRunInspection, type SavedRunListing,
} from '../saved-runs/history.js';
import { terminalText } from './terminal.js';
import { formatWorkerUsage } from './usage.js';

function text(value: string, limit = 4_096): string {
  const safe = terminalText(value).replace(/\s+/gu, ' ').trim();
  return safe.length > limit ? `${safe.slice(0, limit)}… [display shortened]` : safe;
}

export function formatSavedRunLines(run: SavedRunInspection, detail = true): string[] {
  if (run.kind === 'unavailable') {
    return [
      `Run: ${run.runId}`,
      `Status: unavailable (${run.code})`,
      `Continuation blocked: ${inspectionErrorText(run.code)}`,
      'Task, budgets, and approvals are unavailable from a trustworthy record.',
    ];
  }
  const { checkpoint, checks } = run;
  const { state, configuration } = checkpoint;
  const budget = (used: number, allowed: boolean): string => `${used}/2 used; ${allowed ? 2 - used : 0} available${allowed ? '' : ' (worker excluded)'}`;
  const pending = checks.filter((check) => check.status !== 'passed');
  const lines = [
    `Run: ${checkpoint.runId}`,
    `Status: ${checkpoint.status}; updated: ${checkpoint.updatedAt}`,
    `Task (saved): ${text(state.task, detail ? 4_096 : 160)}`,
    `Repo (saved): ${text(checkpoint.repository.root)}`,
    `Iterations: ${run.iterationsUsed}/${checkpoint.iterationLimit} consumed; ${run.iterationsRemaining} remaining`,
    `Codex calls: ${budget(state.codexCalls, configuration.workerSelection !== 'claude')}`,
    `Claude calls: ${budget(state.claudeCalls, configuration.workerSelection !== 'codex')}`,
    formatWorkerUsage(savedWorkerUsage(run.events), 'Saved task worker tokens'),
    `Selection: ${configuration.mode}; ${configuration.provider}/${text(configuration.model)}; worker: ${configuration.workerSelection ?? 'Codex or Claude'}; Codex command network: ${configuration.codexNetworkAccess ? 'enabled' : 'disabled'}`,
    `Pending validation (saved generation ${state.evidence?.validationGeneration ?? 0}): ${pending.map((check) => `${text(check.script)} (${check.status})`).join(', ') || (checks.length ? 'none' : 'no required checks recorded')}`,
    `Last failure: ${run.lastFailure ? text(run.lastFailure, detail ? 1_200 : 300) : 'none recorded'}`,
    ...(run.lastStop ? [`Last stop: ${run.lastStop}`] : []),
    ...(run.recoveryRequired ? ['Recovery: explicit evaluation-failure continuation is still required.'] : []),
    ...run.blockers.map((blocker) => `Continuation blocked: ${blocker}`),
    ...(run.blockers.length === 0 ? ['Continuation: clean stop recorded; repository/configuration review and fresh approvals are still required.'] : []),
  ];
  if (detail) {
    lines.push(
      `Created: ${checkpoint.createdAt}; segments: ${1 + run.events.filter((event) => event.type === 'run_resumed').length}`,
      `Git directory (saved): ${text(checkpoint.repository.gitCommonDirectory)}`,
      `HEAD (saved): ${checkpoint.repository.head}`,
      `Repository availability: ${run.repositoryAvailable ? 'canonical directories available' : 'unavailable'}. HEAD, working files, and current configuration have not been rechecked.`,
      `Independent checks (saved): ${checks.map((check) => `${text(check.script)}: ${check.status}`).join(', ') || 'none recorded'}`,
      'Continuation requires a new validation generation; earlier passes cannot approve completion after restart.',
      `Recent events (${Math.min(run.events.length, SAVED_RUN_TIMELINE_LIMIT)}/${run.events.length}):`,
      ...run.events.slice(-SAVED_RUN_TIMELINE_LIMIT).map((event) => `  ${event.sequence}. ${event.timestamp} ${describeSavedEvent(event)}`),
    );
  }
  return lines;
}

export function formatSavedRunListingLines(listing: SavedRunListing): string[] {
  return [
    ...(listing.total === 0 ? ['No saved runs found.'] : [
      `Showing ${listing.runs.length}/${listing.total} saved runs (unreadable records first, then most recently updated).`,
    ]),
    ...(listing.hiddenRuns ? [`${listing.hiddenRuns} older or additional records are outside this listing.`] : []),
    ...(listing.ignoredEntries ? [`${listing.ignoredEntries} unrecognized store entries were ignored.`] : []),
    'Inspect any known ID, including older records: dev-agent --show-run <run-id> [--plain]',
  ];
}

